{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StylebookAccordion",
  "tagName": "main",
  "$elements": [
    {
      "$ref": "../components/jx-icon.json"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "../components/jx-accordion-item.json"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "../components/jx-accordion.json"
    }
  ],
  "state": {
    "last": "nothing yet",
    "note": {
      "$prototype": "Function",
      "body": [
        {
          "operator": "=",
          "target": {
            "$ref": "#/state/last"
          },
          "value": {
            "$ref": "event#/detail"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "style": {
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
    "color": "var(--jx-fg)",
    "background": "var(--jx-bg)",
    "padding": "var(--jx-space-6)",
    "minHeight": "100vh",
    "& > h1": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-lg)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)"
    },
    "& > h2": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)",
      "margin": "var(--jx-space-5) 0 var(--jx-space-2)"
    },
    "& > p": {
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "tagName": "h1",
      "textContent": "jx-accordion"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "The stack a panel of sections stands in: a column that clips its children's width and draws one hairline BETWEEN them, so a rule falls in every seam and never above the first VISIBLE section. The first stack below opens with a section a panel has bound away, and no hairline is drawn across the top of what is left. The rule is the container's because it is a rule about a child's POSITION among its siblings, which no section can see about itself. Last toggle said: ${state.last}."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "h2",
      "textContent": "A panel of sections"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-accordion",
      "style": {
        "maxWidth": "420px",
        "border": "1px solid var(--jx-border)",
        "borderRadius": "var(--jx-radius-md)",
        "background": "var(--jx-bg-panel)"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "attributes": {
            "hidden": ""
          },
          "$props": {
            "label": "Bound away"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "A panel that binds hidden on a section is why the seam asks for the first VISIBLE child rather than the first child. Unhide this in the inspector and the hairline moves to the section below it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "$props": {
            "label": "Layout",
            "open": true
          },
          "ontoggle": {
            "$ref": "#/state/note"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "Display, position and the box model. The panel's frame is written on the usage site rather than in the element, because a border and a background are this page's idea of a panel and not the stack's."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "$props": {
            "label": "Typography"
          },
          "ontoggle": {
            "$ref": "#/state/note"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "The hairline above this section is the container's rule, and the first section a reader sees has none — the hidden one above it does not count."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "$props": {
            "label": "Nesting"
          },
          "ontoggle": {
            "$ref": "#/state/note"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "A stack inside a section keeps its own seams, because the rule reaches direct children only."
            },
            {
              "tagName": "jx-accordion",
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
                  "$props": {
                    "label": "Inner first"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "p",
                      "textContent": "No rule above this one either."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
                  "$props": {
                    "label": "Inner second"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "p",
                      "textContent": "One seam, in the inner stack."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tagName": "h2",
      "textContent": "One at a time"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "multiple=\"false\" is the container writing down what the panel is for; the platform's own switch is name on each section, and only the section may carry it."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-accordion",
      "$props": {
        "multiple": false
      },
      "style": {
        "maxWidth": "420px",
        "border": "1px solid var(--jx-border)",
        "borderRadius": "var(--jx-radius-md)",
        "background": "var(--jx-bg-panel)"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "$props": {
            "label": "First",
            "name": "stylebook-exclusive",
            "open": true
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "Every item here carries the same name, so the platform closes the others when one opens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-accordion-item",
          "$props": {
            "label": "Second",
            "name": "stylebook-exclusive"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "No shipped Studio panel wants this — all six keep several sections open at once — but the platform gives it for one forwarded attribute."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
